;; bin/javac-vendor ct-sym-own's runner (JCS50 (b), doc/classes/JAVA-CONFORMANCE-SURVEY.md, "As built: JCS50 (b), the own
;; ct.sym"): the JDK build's CreateSymbols (make/langtools/src/classes/build/tools/symbolgenerator, read by repr/java)
;; interpreted on javac's tool executable by gensrc-run.ae, as the own platform's interpreted build tools are:
;;
;;   EXE test/javac-platform/ctsym-run.ae FORMS build.tools.symbolgenerator.CreateSymbols ARG...
;;
;; java.lang.constant.ConstantDescs is initialized first, as a JDK's boot has it before any tool runs (the JDK's own
;; classes use it): java.lang.constant's classes initialize each other in a cycle (ConstantDescs' CD_int is
;; PrimitiveClassDescImpl's, whose constructor reads ConstantDescs' BSM_PRIMITIVE_CLASS and CD_Class), which completes
;; only from ConstantDescs' side; CreateSymbols' first MethodTypeDesc.ofDescriptor would enter it from
;; PrimitiveClassDescImpl's (ExceptionInInitializerError, ConstantDescs' NullPointerException).
(identity java.lang.constant.ConstantDescs/CD_Object)
(load-file (str (.getParent (java.io.File. ^String *file*)) "/gensrc-run.ae"))
